PATIENT VIGNETTE
A 12-year-old boy is brought to the ED by his parents after falling off his bicycle. He was not wearing a helmet and hit his head on the pavement. The boy is conscious and answering questions but complains of a severe headache and nausea. His parents report that he was unconscious for about 30 seconds after the fall. Vital signs: BP 108/72, HR 90, RR 18. No other injuries are noted, and there is no vomiting.

